#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[The Three Engineering Tribes]
<the-three-engineering-tribes>
Physical AI is the meeting ground of three distinct engineering cultures, each bringing indispensable strengths and dangerous blindspots:

- #strong[The Brain (Machine Learning):] Contributes high-capacity foundation models, spatial token representations, and generative trajectory policies. Engineers from this background learn to leave behind the illusion that simulation proves safety, mastering instead complete-path metrology, tail latency budgets, zero-copy Direct Memory Access, and the necessity of isolating neural proposals from physical power stages.
- #strong[The Nervous System (Embedded Systems and Electrical Engineering):] Contributes microsecond clock synchronization, lock-free memory rings, and deterministic scheduling. Engineers from this background learn to move beyond static, hardcoded rules, mastering multi-rate asynchronous message passing and shared SRAM protocols to host multi-gigabyte stochastic models safely alongside real-time loops.
- #strong[The Body (Robotics and Control):] Contributes rigid-body dynamics, invariant safe sets, and physical actuation limits. Engineers from this background learn to move beyond hand-crafted CAD models, mastering the grounding of Vision Transformers and diffusion policies in metric space while caging stochastic proposals within mathematical Control Barrier Functions and thermal energy envelopes.

