- #strong[#ref(<sec-constraints>, supplement: [Chapter]): The Physical Constraints (Time, Inertia, Actuation, Energy, and Silicon):] We measure the five physical and silicon walls that bound intelligent computation: time constants and the freshness wall, inertia and dynamic stopping envelopes ($d_(upright("stop"))$), mechanical actuation rise times and $cal(C)^2$ jerk limits, thermal throttling dissipation ($I^2 R$), and silicon determinism (#NormalTok("malloc=0");).
- #strong[#ref(<sec-cognition>, supplement: [Chapter]): Cognitive Agency (The Five Stages of Physical AI):] We deconstruct the five universal functional stages of physical agency: Perceive ($W_t arrow.r O_t$), Remember ($O_t arrow.r S_t$), Reason ($S_t arrow.r I_t$), Plan ($I_t arrow.r tau_t$), and Execute ($tau_t arrow.r u_t arrow.r W_(t + 1)$), tracing their evolution from classical algorithms to modern foundation models.
