<the-nature-of-physical-agency>
The term #emph[agent] has become ubiquitous across computer science, yet digital agents operating in virtual environments differ fundamentally from physical agents operating in the material world (#ref(<tbl-digital-vs-physical>, supplement: [Table])). Digital agents (such as large language models orchestrating web browsers, code interpreters, or database transactions) operate in forgiving virtual sandboxes. When a digital agent fails, the runtime raises an exception, containerized processes restart, database transactions roll back, and client requests retry without altering the physical state of the universe.

