- #strong[Incident:] Autonomous vehicle struck a pedestrian pushing a cargo-laden bicycle across traffic lanes at full cruising velocity with zero automated braking deceleration applied, dissipating $3.8 times 10^5 upright(" J")$ of kinetic energy in a fatal impact.
- #strong[Telemetry Snapshot:] First detected at $T - 5.6 upright(" s")$ ($82 upright(" m")$ range); classifier toggled across four distinct semantic labels; Kalman filter velocity reset to $upright(bold(0))$ on each label toggle; motion planner asserted $1000 upright(" ms")$ suppression delay at $T - 1.2 upright(" s")$ ($23.3 upright(" m")$ clearance); impact at $T + 0.0 upright(" s")$ ($d_(upright("clearance")) = 0 upright(" m")$).
- #strong[Root Cause:] Semantic label thrashing in the $10 upright(" Hz")$ neural classifier caused the tracking subsystem to repeatedly destruct and re-instantiate C++ tracking objects, zeroing the Kalman filter velocity state vector and hiding lateral motion until an unmanaged $1.0 upright(" s")$ software suppression timer burned the remaining physical dynamic stopping clearance.
- #strong[Architectural Flaw:] Monolithic centralization of safety authority within an asynchronous, class-dependent neural perception pipeline rather than delegating emergency stopping to an independent, class-agnostic 1 kHz bare-metal safety reflex.
