#emph[Why does streaming uncompressed 4K video to improve visual acuity cause an autonomous robot to stumble and crash?]

In digital computer vision, higher resolution is universally celebrated: more pixels yield sharper details and higher accuracy on static benchmarks. In Physical AI, every sensory pixel carries an unyielding physical tax. Streaming multi-camera uncompressed video across a shared System-on-Chip floods dynamic RAM buses, creating memory crossbar contention that chokes neural accelerator weight fetches and explodes inference tail latency. Perception in embodied systems is not passive image classification; it is an active physical pipeline that transforms raw photon fluxes into compact, 3D metric affordance tokens in $S E \( 3 \)$ under strict microsecond budgets before sensory observations decay into spatial uncertainty.

