- #strong[Physical Hazard & Motivation:] Mechanical motor vibration and thermal chassis expansion alter the relative baseline pose between stereo cameras. Treating factory extrinsic calibration as static causes stereo triangulation to hallucinate phantom obstacles or misestimate depth by tens of percent.
- #strong[Variable & Unit Breakdown:]
