- #strong[The Common Assumption:] The spatial extrinsic transformation matrix $upright(bold(T))_(C 1)^(C 2) = \[ upright(bold(R)) divides upright(bold(t)) \] in S E \( 3 \)$ between stereo cameras, or between an exteroceptive camera and the robot kinematic base, can be calibrated to sub-millimeter precision in a factory setting using precision optical targets and locked as static compile-time constants.
