=== The Age of Information (AoI) and Uncertainty Expansion
<the-age-of-information-aoi-and-uncertainty-expansion>
To formally analyze this failure, Physical AI systems model the #strong[Age of Information (AoI)] and the expanding spatial uncertainty envelope:

$ Delta_(upright("AoI")) \( t \) = t - t_(upright("gen")) \( t \) \, #h(2em) sigma_(upright("spatial")) \( t \) = sigma_0 + v_(upright("obs_max")) dot.op Delta_(upright("AoI")) \( t \) $

$ tau_(upright("safe")) = d_(upright("clearance")) / v_(upright("robot")) $

- #strong[Physical Hazard & Motivation:] The moment an optical exposure completes, the observation begins decaying. As latency accumulates across DMA queues and neural layers, the true physical location of dynamic obstacles drifts, expanding spatial uncertainty until safety margins are violated.
- #strong[Variable & Unit Breakdown:]
  - $t_(upright("gen"))$: Physical timestamp when photons struck the camera photodiodes ($upright("s")$).
  - $t$: Current execution timestamp ($upright("s")$).
  - $Delta_(upright("AoI")) \( t \)$: Instantaneous Age of Information ($upright("s")$).
  - $sigma_0$: Baseline sensor measurement uncertainty ($upright("m")$).
  - $v_(upright("obs_max"))$: Maximum dynamic velocity of obstacles in the environment ($upright("m/s")$).
  - $sigma_(upright("spatial")) \( t \)$: Bounding radius of obstacle spatial uncertainty ($upright("m")$).
  - $tau_(upright("safe"))$: Critical freshness expiration deadline ($upright("s")$).
- #strong[Concrete Numerical Example:] For a robot moving at $v_(upright("robot")) = 2.5 upright(" m/s")$ with clearance $d_(upright("clearance")) = 0.15 upright(" m")$, the critical freshness deadline evaluates to $tau_(upright("safe")) = 0.15 / 2.5 = 0.060 upright(" s") = 60 upright(" ms")$. When perception latency inflated to $Delta_(upright("AoI")) = 135 upright(" ms")$, the safety threshold was breached by $75 upright(" ms")$, during which an approaching obstacle ($v_(upright("obs_max")) = 1.0 upright(" m/s")$) expanded spatial uncertainty by $Delta sigma = 1.0 times 0.135 = 13.5 upright(" cm")$. Whenever $Delta_(upright("AoI")) > tau_(upright("safe"))$, the perception organ must mark the observation as expired, triggering downstream planners to discard stale tokens and execute emergency deceleration fallbacks.

