On an embodied physical platform, autoregressive pixel generation is an inefficient architectural choice (#ref(<fig-world-model-paradigms>, supplement: [Figure])):

+ #strong[Computational Arithmetic Overhead:] Generating $1080 upright("p")$ video at 30 FPS requires greater than $10^13 upright(" FLOPs/s")$, saturating dynamic RAM buses and inducing thermal throttling on mobile compute platforms.
+ #strong[Visual Hallucinations:] Pixel decoders frequently synthesize plausible textures while hallucinating nonexistent free space or erasing thin, rigid obstacles. Commanding high-energy actuators based on hallucinated geometry leads directly to structural collisions.
+ #strong[Irrelevant Entropy Consumption:] A pixel-level generative model expends capacity predicting high-frequency visual noise, such as swaying grass, water ripples, or shadow movement, which carries zero functional relevance for physical manipulation.

