#emph[Why does an intelligent foundation model that correctly understands a human voice command instruct a robot arm to break its own joints against a wall?]

Large language and vision-language models possess extraordinary semantic competence to interpret natural language instructions, identify novel objects, and propose strategic task plans. In the physical world, however, pure semantic fluency is dangerously ungrounded: foundation models possess no intrinsic awareness of joint torque limits, link inertia, Jacobian singularities, or physical workspace boundaries. If raw model tokens command actuators directly, the result is mechanical destruction. In Physical AI, foundation models act strictly as untrusted proposal engines emitting time-bounded intent leases ($cal(L)_(upright("intent"))$) screened through kinematic reachability checks and verified by real-time safety enforcers.

