In this incident, the 7-DoF articulated manipulator was deployed in an automated electronics manufacturing facility, equipped with a wrist-mounted RGB-D camera and vacuum tooling (#ref(<fig-intent-platform>, supplement: [Figure])). An operator issued the voice command: #emph["Retrieve the heated calibration bolt behind the fixture."]

The cloud-hosted Vision-Language Model processed the voice audio and camera image, hallucinating a metric target coordinate at $upright(bold(p))_(upright("target")) = \[ 1.32 \, 0.45 \, 0.78 \]^T upright(" m")$ in the robot's base frame, corresponding to a radial distance of:

$ parallel upright(bold(p))_(upright("target")) parallel = sqrt(1.32^2 + 0.45^2 + 0.78^2) = sqrt(2.5533) approx 1.598 upright(" m") approx 1.60 upright(" m") $

The robot's physical reach envelope was strictly bounded by its kinematic link geometry at $R_(upright("max")) = 0.85 upright(" m")$. The commanded goal was $Delta r = 1.59 upright(" m") - 0.85 upright(" m") = 0.74 upright(" m")$ ($74 upright(" cm")$) outside the physical reach envelope.

The software architecture lacked morphological reachability screening, passing the target directly to an unconstrained damped least-squares inverse kinematics solver. Attempting to solve for a Cartesian target $74 upright(" cm")$ beyond the physical workspace boundary drove the kinematic chain into full radial extension, causing the geometric Jacobian matrix $upright(bold(J)) \( upright(bold(q)) \) in bb(R)^(6 times 7)$ to lose rank. Singular value decomposition revealed that the minimum singular value collapsed to $sigma_(upright("min")) \( upright(bold(J)) \) = 0.0004$, causing the Jacobian condition number to explode to:

$ kappa \( upright(bold(J)) \) = frac(sigma_(upright("max")) \( upright(bold(J)) \), sigma_(upright("min")) \( upright(bold(J)) \)) = 0.736 / 0.0004 = 1 \, 840 $

Concurrently, the Yoshikawa manipulability index collapsed to near-zero:

$ w \( upright(bold(q)) \) = sqrt(det (upright(bold(J)) \( upright(bold(q)) \) upright(bold(J))^T \( upright(bold(q)) \))) = product_(i = 1)^6 sigma_i \( upright(bold(J)) \) approx 3.2 times 10^(- 6) lt.double 0.05 $

Because the Cartesian task-space position error $upright(bold(e)) = upright(bold(p))_(upright("target")) - upright(bold(p)) \( upright(bold(q)) \)$ remained large ($parallel upright(bold(e)) parallel = 0.74 upright(" m")$), the inverse kinematic velocity solve commanded extreme joint angular velocities to minimize tracking error:

$ dot(upright(bold(q))) = upright(bold(J))^dagger \( upright(bold(q)) \) dot.op upright(bold(v))_(upright("error")) arrow.r.double.long dot(q)_5 > 450^compose \/ upright("s") quad \( 7.85 upright(" rad/s") \) $

Joint 5 Field-Oriented Control (FOC) motor inverters saturated at maximum stator phase current ($I_(upright("phase")) = 24.0 upright(" A")$), developing peak rated motor torque $tau_(upright("motor")) = K_t dot.op I_(upright("phase")) = 0.25 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m/A") times 24.0 upright(" A") = 6.0 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m")$. Across the $N = 100 : 1$ strain wave gear reduction ratio, the joint delivered a gross output torque of $tau_(upright("out")) approx 600 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m")$, whipping the mechanical forearm across the cell in an uncontrolled arc.

The tool flange struck a $12 upright(" mm")$ structural polycarbonate safety barrier at an impact velocity of $v = 1.4 upright(" m/s")$. Given an effective moving forearm and tool mass of $m_(upright("eff")) approx 4.5 upright(" kg")$ and an elastic contact deformation of $delta approx 2.1 upright(" mm")$ across the barrier over impact duration $Delta t_(upright("impact")) approx 6.0 upright(" ms")$, the dynamic impact force reached:

$ F_(upright("impact")) approx frac(1 / 2 m_(upright("eff")) v^2, delta) = frac(0.5 times 4.5 times \( 1.4 \)^2, 0.0021) = 4.41 / 0.0021 approx 2 \, 100 upright(" N") = 2.1 upright(" kN") $

This impact force reflected through the Joint 5 output flange across a moment arm of $L_(upright("wrist")) = 0.22 upright(" m")$, generating an instantaneous dynamic shock torque of:

$ T_(upright("shock")) = F_(upright("impact")) dot.op L_(upright("wrist")) = 2 \, 100 upright(" N") times 0.22 upright(" m") = 462 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m") $

This shock torque exceeded the size-20 harmonic drive speed reducer's ultimate momentary peak torque rating ($T_(upright("max")) = 250 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m")$) by $85 %$. The thin-walled alloy steel flexspline cup suffered immediate plastic yield and catastrophic tooth shear along its elliptical major axis. The joint locked instantly, cracking the polycarbonate barrier and inflicting $5 \, 400 upright(" USD")$ in replacement hardware and precision laser recalibration costs. The microsecond flight-recorder telemetry ledger is detailed in #ref(<tbl-telemetry-ch07>, supplement: [Table]).

