== Engineering Contract: Intent Lease Schema
<sec-contract-intent>
To guarantee that semantic reasoning foundation models remain strictly bounded within certified physical envelopes, the reasoning subsystem formalizes its output through the #strong[Expiring Intent Lease Interface] (#ref(<tbl-intent-lease>, supplement: [Table])).

Operating at the boundary between System 2 semantic deliberation and System 1.5 trajectory planning, the intent lease operationalizes the Proposal--Permission privilege split. Untrusted foundation models on the host MPU cannot emit raw joint torques, velocity setpoints, or unrestricted Cartesian trajectories. Instead, the model emits an integrity-verified, expiring intent lease packet:

$ cal(L)_(upright("intent")) = chevron.l cal(G)_(upright("task")) \, cal(S)_(upright("hull")) \, t_(upright("issue")) \, Delta t_(upright("lease")) \, upright(bold(w))_(upright("target")) \, cal(B)_(upright("keepout")) \, upright("CRC32") chevron.r $

The lease payload is written into a pinned, zero-copy lock-free ring buffer in coherent shared memory (#NormalTok("dma_alloc_coherent");), stamped with a 64-bit IEEE 1588 PTP hardware timestamp $t_(upright("issue"))$, and protected by a 32-bit CRC checksum. On the downstream real-time microcontroller (ARM Cortex-M7 / R5 / RISC-V), the deterministic permission supervisor evaluates incoming proposals in static SRAM (#NormalTok("malloc = 0");) at $1000 upright(" Hz")$. If any kinematic bound, barrier certificate, or temporal deadline is breached, the supervisor rejects the proposal and commands an autonomous Category 1 controlled deceleration to rest.

