== Incident Autopsy: The Sheared Cycloidal Drive Pin
<sec-cycloidal-autopsy>
The destructive consequence of un-interpolated neural commands is demonstrated in the forensic autopsy of a precision bimanual research manipulator (#ref(<fig-planning-platform>, supplement: [Figure])).

#block[
- #strong[System:] Precision Articulated Bimanual Manipulator ($20 upright(" Hz")$ Diffusion Policy on NVIDIA Jetson AGX Orin, cycloidal speed reducers, $12.0 upright(" kg")$ assembly payload).

- #strong[Incident:] Hardened steel planetary drive pins sheared under an unmitigated chunk seam, mechanically detaching the Joint 2 forearm linkage and dropping a $12.0 upright(" kg")$ fixture payload onto the granite workbench ($3 \, 800 upright(" USD")$ overhaul).

- #strong[Telemetry Snapshot:] At $T + 21.430 upright(" s")$, Chunk $k$ commanded descent ($dot(q)_2 = - 0.42 upright(" rad/s")$); at $T + 21.450 upright(" s")$, Chunk $k + 1$ arrived commanding reversal ($dot(q)_2 = + 0.65 upright(" rad/s")$); at $T + 21.451 upright(" s")$, single-tick drive update commanded $dot.double(q)_2 = 1 \, 070 upright(" rad/s")^2$\; at $T + 21.452 upright(" s")$, motor phase current surged to $28.5 upright(" A")$ delivering $48.2 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m")$ torque shock exceeding $28.0 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m")$ rating; at $T + 21.453 upright(" s")$, pins sheared under $4.2 upright(" kN")$ pin force.

- #strong[Root Cause:] Dispatching discrete neural waypoints across an un-blended chunk seam into a $1.0 upright(" ms")$ motor update loop without $cal(C)^2$ quintic spline interpolation or torque-rate limits, causing an instantaneous acceleration spike ($dot.double(q)_2 = 1 \, 070 upright(" rad/s")^2$) and fatal shear stress ($tau_(upright("pin")) > sigma_(upright("shear"))$).

- #strong[Architectural Flaw:] Absence of a mid-rate trajectory smoothing organ and missing real-time boundary derivative checks, granting un-interpolated neural policy outputs direct motor authority.

- #strong[Provenance:] Forensic analysis of an articulated robotic manipulator transmission failure; flight-recorder telemetry reconstructed for instruction.

