In this incident, the bimanual manipulator was executing an assembly task governed by a $20 upright(" Hz")$ diffusion policy running on an NVIDIA Jetson AGX Orin SoC. The software pipeline dispatched discrete chunk waypoints directly to the motor inverter drives over a CAN-FD bus without intermediate spline interpolation or torque-rate limiting.

During a high-speed downward sweeping motion, Joint 2 reached the boundary of Chunk $k$ at velocity $dot(q)_2 = - 0.42 upright(" rad/s")$. The newly evaluated Chunk $k + 1$ commanded an immediate trajectory reversal, with its initial waypoint specifying $dot(q)_2 = + 0.65 upright(" rad/s")$. Because the low-level motor drive updated its control loop on a $1.0 upright(" ms")$ tick, this commanded an instantaneous velocity jump of $Delta dot(q) = 1.07 upright(" rad/s")$ across a single millisecond.

The commanded acceleration, dynamic torque shock, and pin shear stress follow fundamental mechanics:

$ dot.double(q)_2 = frac(Delta dot(q), Delta t) \, #h(2em) tau_(upright("shock")) = I_(upright("joint2")) dot.op dot.double(q)_2 \, #h(2em) tau_(upright("pin")) = F_(upright("shear")) / A_(upright("pins")) = frac(tau_(upright("shock")) \/ r_(upright("carrier")), n_(upright("pins")) dot.op pi / 4 d_(upright("pin"))^2) $

where:

- $Delta dot(q) = dot(q)_(upright("new")) - dot(q)_(upright("old"))$ is the velocity step across the chunk seam in radians per second ($upright("rad/s")$).
- $Delta t$ is the motor inverter control tick in seconds ($upright("s")$), here $0.001 upright(" s")$ ($1.0 upright(" ms")$).
- $I_(upright("joint2"))$ is the total rotational inertia of the arm linkage and fixture payload in kilogram-meters squared ($upright("kg") dot.op upright("m")^2$).
- $tau_(upright("shock"))$ is the peak dynamic torque impulse in Newton-meters ($upright("N") dot.op upright("m")$).
- $r_(upright("carrier"))$ is the pitch radius of the planetary pin carrier in meters ($upright("m")$).
- $n_(upright("pins"))$ is the number of planetary pins sharing the load, each of diameter $d_(upright("pin"))$.
- $tau_(upright("pin"))$ is the shear stress on the pin cross-section in Megapascals ($upright("MPa")$).

In this incident, commanded acceleration spiked to:

$ dot.double(q)_2 = frac(Delta dot(q), Delta t) = frac(1.07 upright(" rad/s"), 0.001 upright(" s")) = 1 \, 070 upright(" rad/s")^2 $

Given the combined link and payload inertia ($I_(upright("joint2")) approx 0.045 upright(" kg") dot.op upright("m")^2$), the dynamic torque shock was:

$ tau_(upright("shock")) = I_(upright("joint2")) dot.op dot.double(q)_2 = 0.045 times 1 \, 070 = 48.15 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m") approx 48.2 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m") $

This torque pulse exceeded the $28.0 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m")$ rated shear threshold of the Joint 2 cycloidal speed reducer. At a carrier radius of $r_(upright("carrier")) = 0.035 upright(" m")$, total shear force reached $F = 48.15 \/ 0.035 = 1 \, 375.7 upright(" N")$. Concentrated across the pin engagement faces, the peak localized shear stress exceeded the $280 upright(" MPa")$ shear yield strength of the hardened steel pins, shearing them cleanly under $4.2 upright(" kN")$ total instantaneous shear force. The forearm linkage detached and dropped the $12.0 upright(" kg")$ assembly fixture onto the granite table ($3 \, 800 upright(" USD")$ overhaul). The flight-recorder telemetry sequence is documented in #ref(<tbl-telemetry-ch08>, supplement: [Table]).

