=== The Physical Analogy: The Elastic Safety Leash and Minimal Projection
<the-physical-analogy-the-elastic-safety-leash-and-minimal-projection>
To understand the role of the safety filter, consider the mental model of an #strong[Elastic Safety Leash and Minimal-Projection Shield]. When walking an agile, energetic dog, a loose leash allows the animal complete freedom to explore, run, and choose its path. As long as the dog remains on the safe sidewalk, the leash remains completely slack: you exert zero force, preserving $100 %$ of the animal's natural gait and intent.

However, the instant the dog dashes toward the edge of the street, the leash pulls taut at the boundary. Crucially, you do not yank the dog entirely back to the starting line or freeze its legs; you exert only the exact directional tension needed to keep its paws on the sidewalk perimeter.

In Physical AI, the Minimal-Intervention QP acts as this exact elastic leash for generative neural policies:

- #strong[Unconstrained Flow:] As long as the candidate action $upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand"))$ emitted by the neural model satisfies all barrier certificates ($L_f h_i + L_g h_i upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand")) + gamma_i h_i gt.eq 0$), the safety filter is completely passive. The command passes through untouched ($upright(bold(u))^(*) = upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand"))$) in zero solver iterations, preserving the policy's rich behavioral dexterity.
