+ #strong[Physical Hazard:] When an embodied agent detects an obstacle, moving mass continues coasting during computational deliberation and sensor transmission before braking forces can ramp up. If the enforcer sizes clearance only for kinematic braking without accounting for transport latency, this reaction drift will cause high-speed kinetic impacts.

