<contact-impedance-control-and-passivity-energy-tanks>
While rigid position control is effective for free-space motion, it is hazardous during physical contact manipulation and locomotion foot placement. When a manipulator interacts with a rigid surface (such as inserting a component, polishing a workpiece, or contacting an operator), small calibration errors generate extreme contact force spikes: $ F_(upright("contact")) = k_(upright("env")) dot.op Delta x $

