In physical PMSM motors, current flows through three stator coils separated by $120^compose$ electrical phase angles. Trying to regulate rapidly oscillating three-phase sinusoidal AC currents from a stationary frame is like trying to paint a moving horse on a spinning carousel: high rotor speeds induce phase lag and gain attenuation.

