#emph[Why does an autonomous robot that runs flawlessly on the test bench suffer violent latency spikes when deployed inside a sealed chassis?]

In enterprise software architecture, computation is treated as an abstract, fungible commodity: microservices deploy into elastic clusters where physical silicon placement is hidden behind virtualization layers. In Physical AI, silicon topology is an unyielding physical boundary. Moving bits across off-chip memory buses consumes orders of magnitude more electrical energy than arithmetic, shared memory crossbars choke when high-bandwidth camera DMA bursts collide with neural weight streaming, and unmanaged thermal dissipation triggers hardware downclocking that blows past real-time stopping deadlines. Designing an embodied system requires deliberate workload placement---mapping cognitive stages across cloud servers, Linux host processors, neural accelerators, and real-time microcontrollers based on cadence, memory bandwidth, and physical trust boundaries.

