- #strong[The Physical Reality:] Wireless radio frequency (RF) propagation is inherently stochastic. Moving steel machinery, reinforced concrete walls, and insulated panels create RF multipath fading nulls and Faraday shadow blackouts where tail latency spikes beyond $1400 upright(" ms")$ ($P \( upright("blackout") > 1.0 upright(" s") \) > 0$). If a 1.2-ton machine moving at $v = 1.8 upright(" m/s")$ offloads reflex authority to an edge server, an unexpected $1.4 upright(" s")$ network drop results in $2.55 upright(" m")$ of unguided kinetic travel, causing catastrophic impact collisions.
