Analyzing these ripple effects illuminates why physical placement cannot be decoupled from mechanical dynamics:

+ #strong[Cloud Offload Trade-offs:] Maya's desire to offload 70B VLM deliberation to the cloud frees $30 upright(" W")$ of onboard electrical power and extends battery runtime. However, Alex notes that unbuffered 5G latency tails turn wireless packet drops into unguided momentum ($p = m v$). Cloud offloading is only admissible if high-level commands are encapsulated within time-bounded #strong[Expiring Intent Leases] ($tau_(upright("lease")) lt.eq 100 upright(" ms")$), allowing local microcontrollers to safely decelerate if network communication stalls.
+ #strong[Edge NPU Quantization:] Quantizing foundation models into 3B parameter edge variants eliminates external RF dependencies, ensuring complete operational autonomy in RF-shielded environments. However, Carlos and Alex must co-design the physical chassis to dissipate the additional $25 upright(" W")$ of continuous thermal dissipation without triggering DVFS downclocking.
+ #strong[The State Estimation Trap:] Shifting state estimation (such as Kalman filtering or Lie-algebraic pose tracking) from bare-metal microcontrollers to Linux host user-space allows developers to use extensive open-source robotics libraries. However, non-deterministic Linux kernel page faults and thread migrations inject $5 upright("–") 50 upright(" ms")$ of scheduling jitter into the state belief, corrupting numerical velocity derivatives ($dot(upright(bold(x))) approx frac(Delta upright(bold(x)), Delta t)$) and destabilizing high-speed feedback controllers.
+ #strong[The Bare-Metal Reflex Invariant:] Migrating Control Barrier Function Quadratic Programs (CBF-QPs) from Linux to a bare-metal microcontroller reduces safety response latency from $50 upright(" ms")$ down to a deterministic $upright("WCET") lt.eq 175 thin mu upright("s")$, mathematically guaranteeing that safety invariants are enforced even during complete host operating system kernel panics.

The cardinal rule of Physical AI placement dictates: #strong[Never migrate time-critical safety authority across an asynchronous or non-deterministic boundary]. Semantic deliberation may be offloaded to cloud servers if protected by local intent leases, but real-time state estimation and reflex barrier enforcement must remain permanently anchored to local, bare-metal silicon.

#block[
- #strong[The Common Assumption:] If an onboard compute fabric runs out of capacity, dynamically migrating an algorithm (such as point cloud filtering or state estimation) to another onboard core (e.g., from MCU to host Linux MPU) resolves the bottleneck with minimal ripple effect.
- #strong[The Physical Reality:] Re-placing a workload alters memory traffic patterns across the entire shared SoC crossbar. Moving high-rate sensor processing from an isolated SRAM MCU to Linux user-space forces multi-megabyte image and point cloud buffers to traverse the shared LPDDR5 DRAM bus. The resulting bus contention delays NPU weight fetches and inflates camera DMA latency, causing cascading deadline misses in downstream trajectory decoders.
- #strong[The Systems Invariant:] Workload placement across heterogeneous silicon must be statically budgeted and verified across all shared contention domains (DRAM bandwidth, AXI interconnect queues, thermal package limits) using fixed engineering ledgers (#strong[PLACE-01]) before runtime deployment.

] #label("callout-fallacy*-64")
== Incident Autopsy: Cold-Vault Wireless Blackout
<incident-autopsy-cold-vault-wireless-blackout>
The destructive physical reality of offloading time-critical policy execution across a non-deterministic wireless network is documented in the forensic autopsy of an autonomous heavy transport AGV.

