In this industrial incident, a 1.2-ton automated guided vehicle (AGV) was transporting heavy palletized goods across a distribution warehouse at an operational velocity of $v = 1.8 upright(" m/s")$ ($6.48 upright(" km/h")$) (#ref(<fig-agv-mover>, supplement: [Figure])). To minimize onboard thermal dissipation, bill-of-materials cost, and battery consumption, systems architects offloaded the multi-camera vision-language-action (VLA) policy to an offboard edge computing server over a private 5G Ultra-Reliable Low-Latency Communication (URLLC) network.

At timestamp $T + 84.210 upright(" s")$, the AGV crossed the doorway threshold into an industrial cold-storage refrigeration vault. The vault walls were constructed of double-sided steel-clad polyurethane insulation panels, forming a continuous Faraday cage. The RF signal-to-noise ratio collapsed immediately from $+ 24 upright(" dB")$ to $0 upright(" dB")$, and the 5G connection entered an unannounced $1 \, 420 upright(" ms")$ packet blackout.

Onboard the vehicle, the host processor maintained no local trajectory cache. The motor inverter controller was configured with a naive Zero-Order Hold that held the last received torque setpoint ($tau_(upright("motor")) = 240 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m")$) until a new command packet arrived. Lacking an autonomous bare-metal microcontroller evaluating dynamic stopping clearance ($d_(upright("stop"))$) or enforcing hardware heartbeat watchdog timeouts, the 1.2-ton machine coasted forward at full operational velocity:

$ d_(upright("coast")) = v dot.op Delta t_(upright("blackout")) = 1.80 upright(" m/s") times 1.420 upright(" s") = 2.556 upright(" m") $

At the entrance of the vault, a structural steel building column was located at a physical clearance of $d_(upright("clearance")) = 1.200 upright(" m")$. Because the vehicle traveled $2.556 upright(" m")$ without initiating deceleration, it completely exhausted the available clearance buffer and overshot the impact point by:

$ Delta d = d_(upright("coast")) - d_(upright("clearance")) = 2.556 upright(" m") - 1.200 upright(" m") = + 1.356 upright(" m") $

The vehicle struck the solid steel column at full operational velocity ($v = 1.80 upright(" m/s")$). With a total vehicle mass of $m = 1 \, 200 upright(" kg")$, the linear momentum carried into the collision was:

$ p = m v = 1 \, 200 upright(" kg") times 1.80 upright(" m/s") = 2 \, 160 upright(" kg") dot.op upright("m/s") = 2.16 times 10^3 upright(" N") dot.op upright("s") $

The kinetic energy dissipated during impact was:

$ E_k = 1 / 2 m v^2 = 1 / 2 times 1 \, 200 upright(" kg") times \( 1.80 upright(" m/s") \)^2 = 1 \, 944 upright(" Joules") $

The structural deceleration shock sheared the $45 upright(" mm")$ alloy-steel front steering kingpin, ruptured the $210 upright(" bar")$ high-pressure hydraulic steering lines, and crushed the forward $48 upright(" V")$ lithium iron phosphate ($upright("LiFePO")_4$) battery modules ($42 \, 000 upright(" USD")$ overhaul cost). The flight-recorder telemetry ledger is detailed in #ref(<tbl-telemetry-ch10>, supplement: [Table]).

