== Systems Stress-Tests: Architectural Food for Thought
<systems-stress-tests-architectural-food-for-thought-5>
Evaluating heterogeneous compute placement across physical embodiments requires confronting multi-dimensional trade-offs where statistical foundation model capacity, silicon memory bus physics, and thermal thermodynamics intersect. The following four architectural stress-tests examine critical edge cases across heterogeneous silicon placement:

#heading(level: 4, numbering: none)[Stress-Test 1: Cloud 70B Foundation Generalization vs.~The Wireless Multipath Drop]
<stress-test-1-cloud-70b-foundation-generalization-vs.-the-wireless-multipath-drop>
An engineering team is deploying a fleet of $800 upright(" kg")$ autonomous mobile tugs in a high-density manufacturing facility. The team must choose between:

+ #strong[Architecture A (Offboard 70B Cloud Model):] Streams compressed stereo video over a private 5G URLLC network ($P_50 = 4 upright(" ms")$ RTT), unlocking open-world zero-shot semantic task reasoning and rich multi-modal failure recovery.
+ #strong[Architecture B (Onboard 3B Quantized Edge Model):] Runs an INT8-quantized model locally on an embedded 30 W SoC ($T_(upright("infer")) = 350 upright(" ms")$), with lower open-world generalization but zero RF dependency.

During initial testing of Architecture A, a tug traveling at $v = 2.0 upright(" m/s")$ enters an aisle lined with structural steel beams and metal mesh shelving. Multipath RF reflections create a destructive interference null, triggering an unannounced $920 upright(" ms")$ 5G packet blackout.

#emph[If Architecture A is deployed, what exact mathematical lease mechanism and local microcontroller stopping envelope ($d_(upright("stop"))$) must be implemented to prevent the tug from coasting unguided into pedestrians during the $920 upright(" ms")$ blackout? At what vehicle velocity and spatial clearance boundary does offboard cloud deliberation become physically unsafe regardless of wireless network QoS?]

#heading(level: 4, numbering: none)[Stress-Test 2: On-Chip SRAM Weight Tiling vs.~LPDDR5 Memory Crossbar Saturation]
<stress-test-2-on-chip-sram-weight-tiling-vs.-lpddr5-memory-crossbar-saturation>
A bimanual humanoid robot is designed to execute high-speed reactive manipulation ($50 upright(" Hz")$ trajectory generation). The System 1.5 diffusion policy requires evaluating a 1D Temporal U-Net backbone on an embedded SoC.

The engineering team has two options:

+ #strong[Option 1 (Large 65 MB FP16 Model on DRAM):] Generates exceptionally dexterous trajectories across 12 contact stages, but requires fetching $65 upright(" MB")$ of weights from LPDDR5 DRAM per forward pass ($3.25 upright(" GB/s")$ continuous DRAM traffic).
+ #strong[Option 2 (Compact 6.5 MB INT8 Model in SRAM):] Quantized to fit entirely within the NPU's dedicated $8 upright(" MB")$ on-chip static SRAM ($I_(upright("arith")) > 180 upright(" FLOPs/Byte")$, zero DRAM traffic), with a $4 %$ reduction in trajectory success rate on delicate assembly tasks.

Bench testing reveals that under Option 1, the continuous DRAM weight fetches saturate the shared 128-bit memory crossbar, contending with three 4K camera DMA streams. Memory controller queues back up, inflating MCU state-read latency from $45 upright(" ns")$ to $1.2 thin mu upright("s")$ and causing the 1 kHz safety enforcer to miss its timer interrupt deadline on $0.8 %$ of cycles.

#emph[How should systems engineers structure AXI Quality-of-Service (#NormalTok("ARQOS");/#NormalTok("AWQOS");) arbitration registers and memory bus partitioning to guarantee hard real-time execution while maximizing neural model capacity? Under what operational conditions is the $4 %$ algorithmic accuracy loss of Option 2 strictly required for hardware survival?]

#heading(level: 4, numbering: none)[Stress-Test 3: The Sealed IP67 Conduction Chassis and the DVFS Thermal Cliff]
<stress-test-3-the-sealed-ip67-conduction-chassis-and-the-dvfs-thermal-cliff>
An autonomous inspection rover operating in a chemical processing plant is housed in an IP67 hermetically sealed aluminum chassis without external cooling fans. The ambient temperature is $T_(upright("ambient")) = 45^compose upright("C")$. The thermal resistance of the enclosure is $R_(upright("th")) = 1.80 upright(" K/W")$, and the lumped thermal capacitance is $C_(upright("th")) = 25.0 upright(" J/K")$ ($tau_(upright("th")) = 45 upright(" s")$).

The onboard edge SoC dissipates $P_(upright("total")) = 25.0 upright(" W")$ during continuous high-cadence neural inference ($50 upright(" Hz")$, $H = 16$). After 98 seconds of operation, junction temperature breaches the silicon safety limit ($T_j > 85^compose upright("C")$). The on-chip hardware power manager triggers Dynamic Voltage and Frequency Scaling (DVFS), downclocking the NPU clock from $1.2 upright(" GHz")$ to $480 upright(" MHz")$ ($0.40 times$). Forward inference latency explodes from $22 upright(" ms")$ to $55 upright(" ms")$, missing the $50 upright(" ms")$ action chunking deadline and causing the vehicle to trip an emergency stop mid-mission.

#emph[How should the system's runtime firmware implement Proactive Thermal Cadence Scaling (e.g., dynamically transitioning from $50 upright(" Hz")$ to $20 upright(" Hz")$ and expanding horizon from $H = 16$ to $H = 32$ at $T_j gt.eq 75^compose upright("C")$) to achieve steady-state thermal equilibrium without sacrificing kinematic tracking accuracy?]

#heading(level: 4, numbering: none)[Stress-Test 4: Lock-Free SRAM IPC vs.~Non-Coherent Cache Line Invalidation Overhead]
<stress-test-4-lock-free-sram-ipc-vs.-non-coherent-cache-line-invalidation-overhead>
A heterogeneous robotic compute architecture transfers high-rate trajectory chunks between an 8-core 64-bit ARM Cortex-A78 application processor (Linux host) and a dual-core lockstep ARM Cortex-M7 microcontroller (real-time safety executive) across a shared on-chip SRAM mailbox.

Because the Cortex-A78 operates with hierarchical L1/L2 data caches while the Cortex-M7 accesses tightly coupled DTCM SRAM without hardware cache snooping, the memory interface is non-coherent. To transfer a 2 KB trajectory chunk at $100 upright(" Hz")$, the Linux driver must execute an explicit cache clean operation (#NormalTok("clean_dcache_range");), and the MCU must execute a cache invalidate operation (#NormalTok("invalidate_dcache_range");) to the Point of Coherency (PoC).

Under heavy multi-threaded Linux workloads, cache line invalidations stall the CPU pipeline and incur memory bus flush penalties that inflate average IPC handoff latency from $2.5 thin mu upright("s")$ to $180 thin mu upright("s")$, with $P_99$ latency spikes exceeding $850 thin mu upright("s")$.

#emph[How must systems architects organize shared memory layouts, cache line padding (#NormalTok("alignas(64)");), and atomic acquire-release sequence counters to achieve microsecond-deterministic zero-copy IPC across non-coherent processor cores without risking torn reads or pipeline stalls?]

== Chapter Summary and Forward Handoff to #ref(<sec-governance>, supplement: [Chapter])
<chapter-summary-and-forward-handoff-to-sec-governance>
This chapter established how cognitive workloads are deliberately placed across heterogeneous silicon fabrics. Physical AI rejects the cloud illusion of fungible compute, mapping multi-rate cognitive stages across Cloud, Host MPU, Neural Accelerator NPU, and Real-Time MCU based on cadence ($0.001 upright(" Hz") arrow.r 1000 upright(" Hz")$), memory bandwidth, thermal dissipation, and physical trust boundaries.

The architectural discipline of heterogeneous compute placement rests on three core pillars:

+ #strong[Non-Fungibility of Physical Silicon:] Time-critical safety loops ($1000 upright(" Hz")$) cannot be offloaded across non-deterministic wireless networks (5G/Wi-Fi) or general-purpose operating system schedulers. Generative policies propose candidate trajectories under expiring #strong[Intent Leases] ($tau_(upright("lease")) lt.eq 100 upright(" ms")$), while bare-metal microcontrollers maintain exclusive hardware authority over motor inverters.
+ #strong[Deterministic Interconnects and Zero-Copy IPC:] Shared Unified Memory Architectures (UMA) require hardware #strong[AXI QoS Priority Arbitration] (#NormalTok("QoS=15"); for MCU, #NormalTok("QoS=10"); for NPU, #NormalTok("QoS=4"); for Camera DMA) to prevent video streams from starving real-time control loops. Inter-processor communication must use lock-free SRAM ring buffers with strict 64-byte cache line isolation (#NormalTok("alignas(64)");) to eliminate mutex context switching and cache line ping-pong.
+ #strong[Thermodynamic Co-Design & Arithmetic Intensity:] Moving bits across off-chip DRAM consumes $750 times$ more energy per byte than on-chip arithmetic ($150 upright(" pJ")$ vs $0.2 upright(" pJ")$). Quantizing trajectory models to reside permanently in on-chip SRAM ($I_(upright("arith")) gt.eq 120 upright(" FLOPs/Byte")$) eliminates DRAM bus heating. Real-time proactive thermal cadence scaling dynamically adjusts chunk horizons ($H = 16 arrow.r 32$) and inference rates ($50 upright(" Hz") arrow.r 20 upright(" Hz")$) at $T_j gt.eq 75^compose upright("C")$, preventing catastrophic DVFS downclocking cliffs ($> 85^compose upright("C")$).

=== Advancing to #ref(<sec-governance>, supplement: [Chapter]): Runtime Governance and Safety Systems
<advancing-to-sec-governance-runtime-governance-and-safety-systems>
