In #ref(<sec-governance>, supplement: [Chapter]), we explore how distributed physical agents are governed during continuous operations:

- #strong[Dual-Heartbeat Hardware Watchdogs:] Structuring bidirectional hardware and software heartbeats between Linux host MPUs and bare-metal MCUs to detect hung threads and trigger microsecond safety fallbacks.
- #strong[Dynamic Hazard Escalation:] Implementing multi-tier fallback hierarchies (Category 2 trajectory hold $arrow.r$ Category 1 controlled deceleration $arrow.r$ Category 0 hardware Safe Torque Off) governed by runtime safety monitors.
- #strong[Expiring Intent Lease Protocols:] Enforcing bounded execution leases that automatically safe the platform when semantic planners fail to refresh commands within their allocated latency budget.
- #strong[Governed Data Flywheels:] Capturing real-world failure edge cases and out-of-distribution physical interactions for fleet-level retraining while preserving runtime determinism and operational safety.

