=== Forensic Disciplinary Autopsy
<forensic-disciplinary-autopsy>
The investigation revealed how subtle oversights compounded across disciplines:

- #strong[Maya's CS/ML Diagnosis:] The behavioral cloning loss function converged to near-zero training error on the cloud GPU cluster. Because the model was evaluated on offline held-out validation trajectories that contained the exact same un-tagged human emergency swerves, traditional ML validation metrics ($R^2$, MSE) appeared exceptional. The validation set did not penalize the model for driving toward pillars because it rewarded matching the human swerve at the end of the drift.
- #strong[Carlos's ECE/Embedded Diagnosis:] The microcontroller firmware had a register flag indicating joystick override, but the serialization struct in the shared-memory ring buffer omitted this bit to save 4 bytes of DMA bandwidth. The Linux telemetry daemon streamed raw $\( s \, a \)$ tuples to the cloud without the non-forgeable $upright(bold(1))_(upright("human_active"))$ flag, blinding the data pipeline to human interventions.
- #strong[Alex's MechE/Robotics Diagnosis:] When the delayed turn failed, the vehicle's dynamic stopping envelope ($d_(upright("stop")) = 1.20 upright(" m")$) was fully exhausted. The rigid $1 \, 200 upright(" kg")$ chassis impacted the $500 upright(" mm")$ reinforced concrete column at $1.8 upright(" m/s")$, shearing mounting bolts, bending the fork mast by $14^compose$, and transferring an instantaneous impulse of $> 2 \, 000 upright(" N") dot.op upright("s")$ into building structural footings.

