=== Dual-Bank A/B Firmware Governance and Watchdog Rollback
<dual-bank-ab-firmware-governance-and-watchdog-rollback>
A critical requirement of GOV-01 is #strong[Dual-Bank A/B Firmware Governance]. When deploying over-the-air (OTA) updates to fleet robots, the bare-metal microcontroller memory is partitioned into two independent physical flash banks (Bank A and Bank B). The new firmware binary is written to the inactive bank while the machine operates normally from the active bank.

Upon reboot, the hardware bootloader performs cryptographic signature verification using Ed25519 public keys. It boots into the new partition and arms an independent $50 upright(" ms")$ hardware watchdog timer. The newly booted firmware must complete self-tests, verify memory invariants, and successfully exchange its first safety heartbeats with low-level inverter drivers before strobing the watchdog clear line. If a null pointer dereference, memory overflow, or control loop deadline miss occurs during startup, the watchdog timer expires, automatically reverting the boot vector back to the golden Bank A partition within $< 50 upright(" ms")$, ensuring zero fleet bricking in the field.

