#strong[The Physical Failure:] An instantaneous setpoint switch commands infinite torque derivatives ($dot(bold(tau)) arrow.r oo$). Inverter gate drivers saturate at peak current limits, exciting torsional resonance and injecting severe dynamic shock loads ($> 60 \, 000 upright(" N") dot.op upright("m/s")$) across precision cycloidal and harmonic drive transmissions. Over multiple interventions, these shock loads induce surface micro-pitting, flexspline fatigue, and tooth shear.

