In automotive engineering, crash sleds subject restraint control modules to $50 g$ deceleration pulses with intentionally severed CAN bus wires to prove that airbag squibs fire deterministically. In aerospace propulsion, Full Authority Digital Engine Control (FADEC) certification benches inject simulated lightning surges on 28V DC power rails, microsecond fuel pressure drops, and air bubbles into high-pressure pumps, proving that backup channels take over in $< 10 upright(" ms")$ with zero engine flameout.

Physical AI release qualification requires subjecting the integrated System-on-Chip and microcontroller testbed to automated #strong[Cross-Layer Seeded Fault Injection] (#ref(<fig-cross-layer-faults>, supplement: [Figure])).

