#strong[The Fallacy:] Achieving a $99.9 %$ task success rate across $100 \, 000$ hours of domain-randomized physics simulation provides sufficient evidence to release an autonomous physical agent.

#strong[The Physical Reality:] Physics simulators do not model rolling shutter shear, memory crossbar contention, PTP clock skew, or thermal demagnetization. High simulation accuracy demonstrates algorithmic convergence in virtual time, not physical safety on target silicon. Hardware-in-the-Loop fault injection on physical silicon is indispensable @leveson2011engineering.

