The assurance discipline rests on three core pillars:

+ #strong[Bounded Operational Design Domains:] Physical agents operate safely only within mathematically explicit environmental, kinematic, and sensor boundaries ($cal(X)_(upright("ODD"))$). Breaching these envelopes triggers immediate, deterministic fallback stops.
+ #strong[The 4-Rung Qualification Ladder:] Progressing candidate policies from historical replay to domain-randomized simulation, hardware-in-the-loop silicon emulation, and real-world shadow fleet validation eliminates blindspots before physical motors receive actuation authority.
