- #strong[The Common Assumption:] Increasing parameter counts ($N$) and compute FLOPs ($C$) on unconstrained transformer architectures will automatically yield physical common sense, dexterous contact manipulation, and universal robotic generalization.

- #strong[The Physical Reality:] Web-scale text tokens are virtual and unconstrained, but physical space is strictly bounded by the Euclidean Lie group $S E \( 3 \) = S O \( 3 \) times.l bb(R)^3$, conservation of momentum, and thermal limits. An unconstrained 70B transformer requires tens of thousands of real-world physical trials simply to learn rotational symmetry, while dissipating excessive Joulean power in memory crossbars and suffering multi-hundred-millisecond inference latency tails.

- #strong[The Systems Invariant:] Physical AI foundation models must incorporate inductive geometric biases (such as $S E \( 3 \)$-equivariant network layers and Hamiltonian or Lagrangian energy constraints), reducing physical sample complexity by more than $100 times$ while keeping model parameter footprints small enough to execute within embedded edge memory envelopes.

