where $bold(lambda) in bb(R)^K$ is the vector of non-negative Lagrange multipliers. The Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) optimality conditions are:

+ #strong[Stationarity:] $nabla_(upright(bold(u))) cal(L) = upright(bold(W)) \( upright(bold(u))^(*) - upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand")) \) - upright(bold(A))^T bold(lambda)^(*) = upright(bold(0)) arrow.r.double.long upright(bold(u))^(*) = upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand")) + upright(bold(W))^(- 1) upright(bold(A))^T bold(lambda)^(*)$
+ #strong[Primal Feasibility:] $upright(bold(A)) upright(bold(u))^(*) - upright(bold(b)) gt.eq upright(bold(0))$
+ #strong[Dual Feasibility:] $bold(lambda)^(*) gt.eq upright(bold(0))$
+ #strong[Complementary Slackness:] $lambda_k^(*) \( upright(bold(a))_k^T upright(bold(u))^(*) - b_k \) = 0 \, quad forall k in { 1 \, dots.h \, K }$

Let $cal(A) subset.eq { 1 \, dots.h \, K }$ denote the active constraint set at the optimal solution (where $upright(bold(a))_k^T upright(bold(u))^(*) = b_k$ and $lambda_k^(*) > 0$). Restricting $upright(bold(A))$ and $upright(bold(b))$ to the active rows $upright(bold(A))_(cal(A))$:

$ upright(bold(A))_(cal(A)) upright(bold(u))^(*) = upright(bold(A))_(cal(A)) (upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand")) + upright(bold(W))^(- 1) upright(bold(A))_(cal(A))^T bold(lambda)_(cal(A))^(*)) = upright(bold(b))_(cal(A)) $

Rearranging yields the symmetric positive-definite active-set linear system for the optimal dual variables:

$ (upright(bold(A))_(cal(A)) upright(bold(W))^(- 1) upright(bold(A))_(cal(A))^T) bold(lambda)_(cal(A))^(*) = upright(bold(b))_(cal(A)) - upright(bold(A))_(cal(A)) upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand")) $

Solving for $bold(lambda)_(cal(A))^(*)$ via Cholesky decomposition $upright(bold(L)) upright(bold(L))^T = upright(bold(A))_(cal(A)) upright(bold(W))^(- 1) upright(bold(A))_(cal(A))^T$, the optimal projected control command is:

$ upright(bold(u))^(*) = upright(bold(u))_(upright("cand")) + upright(bold(W))^(- 1) upright(bold(A))_(cal(A))^T bold(lambda)_(cal(A))^(*) $

#heading(level: 3, numbering: none)[Microcontroller Real-Time Solvers and Complexity Bounds]
