On safety-critical microcontrollers (such as a dual-core lockstep ARM Cortex-M7 at $480 upright(" MHz")$), solving the active-set CBF-QP is executed using static memory allocations in Data Tightly-Coupled Memory (DTCM) with zero heap fragmentation (#NormalTok("malloc = 0");).

