$ dot(upright(bold(x))) \( t \) = f \( upright(bold(x)) \( t \) \, upright(bold(u)) \( t \) \) + upright(bold(w)) \( t \) \, #h(2em) upright(bold(w)) \( t \) tilde.op cal(N) \( upright(bold(0)) \, upright(bold(Q))_c \( t \) \) $

The estimated state mean propagates via the nominal dynamics:

$ dot(hat(upright(bold(x)))) \( t \) = f \( hat(upright(bold(x))) \( t \) \, upright(bold(u)) \( t \) \) $

Defining estimation error $upright(bold(e)) \( t \) = upright(bold(x)) \( t \) - hat(upright(bold(x))) \( t \)$ and linearizing $f \( upright(bold(x)) \, upright(bold(u)) \)$ via Taylor expansion about $hat(upright(bold(x))) \( t \)$:

$ f \( upright(bold(x)) \( t \) \, upright(bold(u)) \( t \) \) = f \( hat(upright(bold(x))) \( t \) \, upright(bold(u)) \( t \) \) + upright(bold(F)) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \) + cal(O) \( parallel upright(bold(e)) parallel^2 \) \, #h(2em) upright(bold(F)) \( t \) = frac(partial f, partial upright(bold(x)))\|_(hat(upright(bold(x))) \( t \) \, upright(bold(u)) \( t \)) $

The continuous error dynamics satisfy:

$ dot(upright(bold(e))) \( t \) = dot(upright(bold(x))) \( t \) - dot(hat(upright(bold(x)))) \( t \) = upright(bold(F)) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \) + upright(bold(w)) \( t \) $

The spatial error covariance matrix is defined as the expectation $upright(bold(P)) \( t \) = bb(E) \[ upright(bold(e)) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \)^T \]$. Applying the product rule for differentiation:

$ dot(upright(bold(P))) \( t \) = frac(d, d t) bb(E) \[ upright(bold(e)) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \)^T \] = bb(E) \[ dot(upright(bold(e))) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \)^T \] + bb(E) \[ upright(bold(e)) \( t \) dot(upright(bold(e))) \( t \)^T \] $

Substituting the error differential equation:

$ bb(E) \[ dot(upright(bold(e))) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \)^T \] = bb(E) \[ \( upright(bold(F)) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \) + upright(bold(w)) \( t \) \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \)^T \] = upright(bold(F)) \( t \) upright(bold(P)) \( t \) + bb(E) \[ upright(bold(w)) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \)^T \] $

Because white Gaussian process noise $upright(bold(w)) \( t \)$ is uncorrelated with past estimation errors, $bb(E) \[ upright(bold(w)) \( t \) upright(bold(e)) \( t \)^T \] = 1 / 2 upright(bold(Q))_c \( t \)$. Adding the transpose term yields the #strong[Continuous Matrix Riccati Differential Equation]:

$ dot(upright(bold(P))) \( t \) = upright(bold(F)) \( t \) upright(bold(P)) \( t \) + upright(bold(P)) \( t \) upright(bold(F)) \( t \)^T + upright(bold(Q))_c \( t \) $

Discretizing across integration time step $Delta t = 1.0 upright(" ms")$:

$ hat(upright(bold(x)))_(k \| k - 1) = hat(upright(bold(x)))_(k - 1 \| k - 1) + integral_(t_(k - 1))^(t_k) f \( hat(upright(bold(x))) \( tau \) \, upright(bold(u))_(k - 1) \) thin d tau approx hat(upright(bold(x)))_(k - 1 \| k - 1) + f \( hat(upright(bold(x)))_(k - 1 \| k - 1) \, upright(bold(u))_(k - 1) \) Delta t $

$ upright(bold(P))_(k \| k - 1) = bold(Phi)_k upright(bold(P))_(k - 1 \| k - 1) bold(Phi)_k^T + upright(bold(Q))_d $

where $bold(Phi)_k approx upright(bold(I)) + upright(bold(F)) \( t_(k - 1) \) Delta t$ is the state transition matrix and $upright(bold(Q))_d approx upright(bold(Q))_c Delta t$ is discrete process noise covariance.

