In embedded motion controllers, calculating the $6 times n$ Geometric Jacobian $upright(bold(J)) \( upright(bold(q)) \)$, Yoshikawa manipulability $w \( upright(bold(q)) \) = sqrt(det \( upright(bold(J)) upright(bold(J))^T \))$, and condition metric $kappa \( upright(bold(J)) \)$ is performed using static array allocations in SRAM with zero dynamic memory allocation (#NormalTok("malloc = 0");).

