$ I_(upright("arith")) = N_(upright("FLOPs")) / N_(upright("Bytes_DRAM")) quad [upright("FLOPs") / upright("Byte")] $

Total electrical power dissipated by the compute subsystem $P_(upright("compute"))$ is the sum of dynamic gate switching power, static transistor leakage, and DRAM bus input/output pad driving power:

$ P_(upright("compute")) = P_(upright("dynamic")) + P_(upright("leakage")) + P_(upright("DRAM_IO")) $

$ P_(upright("dynamic")) = alpha dot.op C_(upright("eff")) dot.op V_(upright("core"))^2 dot.op f_(upright("clock")) $

$ P_(upright("DRAM_IO")) = E_(upright("DRAM_byte")) dot.op upright("BW")_(upright("DRAM")) = E_(upright("DRAM_byte")) dot.op upright("Throughput")_(upright("FLOPs/s")) / I_(upright("arith")) $

where $E_(upright("DRAM_byte")) approx 150 upright(" pJ/Byte")$ for off-chip LPDDR5 DRAM, compared to $E_(upright("SRAM_byte")) approx 2 upright(" pJ/Byte")$ for on-chip static SRAM.

